00:22:26.360 --> 00:22:28.040
a brainstorming session.
一场头脑风暴会议。

443
00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:33.980
Oh, lady, there is a scene between Jim and Pam that is not in this episode.
哦，天哪，吉姆和帕姆之间有一场戏并不在这一集里。

444
00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:35.700
And it's not in the deleted scene.
而且也不在删减片段里。

445
00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.180
So you have to tell me if you guys film this.
所以你得告诉我你们当时到底有没有拍过。

446
00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:39.460
It's kind of racy.
那场戏有点大胆。

447
00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:40.480
You want to hear it?
你想听听吗？

448
00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:41.460
What?
什么？

449
00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:44.440
So I'm reading the shooting draft last night.
昨晚我在读拍摄剧本。

450
00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:45.800
And this is in there.
里面就有这一段。

451
00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:49.460
As people head to the conference room, Jim smiles at Pam.
当大家走向会议室时，吉姆向帕姆微笑。

452
00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:52.880
Jim says, the price you pay for a night in heaven.
吉姆说，这就是在天堂共度一夜的代价。

453
00:22:53.860 --> 00:22:54.720
Oh, wait.
噢，等等。

454
00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:58.120
Pam glances at the camera, stilted.
帕姆瞥了一眼镜头，显得有些局促。

455
00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:01.740
Yes, the movies were good, Jim.
没错，电影很棒，吉姆。

456
00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:06.500
Jim says, you mean the movies that we made of us making love?
吉姆说，你是说我们拍的那些亲热的电影吗？

457
00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:11.320
Glances to camera.
瞥向镜头。

458
00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:12.480
Shut up.
闭嘴。

459
00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:14.160
We didn't film ourselves.
我们没拍过自己。

460
00:23:14.720 --> 00:23:15.900
Jim to camera.
吉姆看向镜头。

461
00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:17.880
Hi, Pam's grandma.
嗨，帕姆的奶奶。

462
00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:19.740
Sorry you had to find out like this.
很抱歉让你以这种方式发现。

463
00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:23.340
And then Pam hits Jim and they go into the conference room.
然后帕姆打了吉姆一下，他们一起走进会议室。

464
00:23:23.860 --> 00:23:24.180
What?
什么？

465
00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:28.180
I don't remember if we filmed that.
我不记得我们有没有拍过那个。

466
00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:30.640
If it's in the shooting draft, we must have.
如果剧本初稿里有，那我们肯定拍了。

467
00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:34.060
People would have lost their minds if we'd left that in the show.
如果那段被剪进正片里，大家肯定会疯掉的。

468
00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:35.260
I know.
我知道。

469
00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:37.280
Like, what the heck?
就像是，搞什么鬼？

470
00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:40.500
I read it last night and I was like, like I did a spit take.
我昨晚读到的时候，简直喷了出来。

471
00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:42.340
I was like, what's happening with Jim and Pam?
我当时心想，吉姆和帕姆这是怎么了？

472
00:23:42.780 --> 00:23:46.800
Just hearing that makes me feel like I've just walked in on my parents.
光是听到这些，就让我感觉像是撞见了父母。

473
00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:47.700
I know.
我知道。

474
00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:49.560
Having an intimate moment.
正在亲热。

475
00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:52.080
Like, I was just like, no, no, no, don't want to see it.
我当时就是，不，不，不，我不想看。

476
00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:52.900
Don't want to see it.
不想看。

477
00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:56.400
Which is probably why it was edited out.
这大概就是它被剪掉的原因。

478
00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:58.740
But it cracked me up reading it.
但读到的时候确实把我逗乐了。

479
00:23:59.740 --> 00:23:59.980
Wow.
哇。

480
00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.240
Well, there you go, guys.
好吧，就是这样，伙计们。

481
00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:04.280
There you go.
就是这样。

482
00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:08.300
Now we're in the conference room and the actual scene they leave in between the two of you guys
现在我们到了会议室，你们俩之间留下的那场戏

483
00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:11.820
is Jim proposing to Pam, which is also in the script.
是吉姆向帕姆求婚，那也在剧本里。

484
00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:16.440
So I guess if they had to choose one, that one is a little bit more in character for you guys.
所以我猜如果必须二选一，那场戏更符合你们的人设。

485
00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:19.860
Well, proposing that I go get him some more coffee.
好吧，求婚的内容是我去给他再倒杯咖啡。

486
00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:21.060
Right, right, right.
对，对，对。

487
00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:22.140
But you're doing the thing.
但你现在在配合他。

488
00:24:22.280 --> 00:24:24.820
You know, he's now doing this bit with you, right?
你知道，他现在在跟你演这出戏，对吧？

489
00:24:25.540 --> 00:24:25.860
Yeah.
是啊。

490
00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:32.060
Well, Michael has written the words energize in block letters on a piece of paper up front.
迈克尔在前面的纸上用大写字母写下了“注入活力”几个字。

491
00:24:32.060 --> 00:24:37.140
And he wants to know, how can we energize the office?
他想知道，我们该如何为办公室注入活力？

492
00:24:37.580 --> 00:24:39.620
A few people are throwing out ideas.
几个人正在提出建议。

493
00:24:39.880 --> 00:24:45.400
Andy suggests that we have a new outgoing message, something with zing and pep.
安迪建议我们换个新的语音留言，要更有活力和干劲。

494
00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:51.800
Jim suggests we have an even better message with more zing and more pep.
吉姆建议我们换个更好的留言，要有更多的活力和干劲。

495
00:24:52.160 --> 00:24:54.740
Michael wants to get Stanley's opinion.
迈克尔想听听斯坦利的意见。

496
00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:56.420
Stanley's not having it.
斯坦利根本不理会。

497
00:24:56.520 --> 00:24:57.740
He's like, not me.
他就像是说，别找我。

498
00:24:58.020 --> 00:24:59.000
He's not interested.
他没兴趣。

499
00:24:59.140 --> 00:25:00.360
He's not even answering him.
他甚至都不回答他。

500
00:25:00.360 --> 00:25:01.000
I know.
我知道。

501
00:25:01.220 --> 00:25:04.260
And Michael keeps pushing and pushing and pushing.
而迈克尔还在不停地施压，不停地施压，不停地施压。

502
00:25:04.660 --> 00:25:07.140
And that is when he says the line,
就在那时，他说出了那句台词，

503
00:25:07.560 --> 00:25:09.740
Did I stutter?
我结巴了吗？

504
00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:12.140
And everyone is stunned.
所有人都惊呆了。

505
00:25:12.460 --> 00:25:15.400
We're like, whoa, this just took a turn.
我们当时心想，哇，这下情况不对劲了。

506
00:25:15.920 --> 00:25:18.780
Michael excuses himself for a glass of water.
迈克尔找借口去倒杯水。

507
00:25:19.280 --> 00:25:19.900
Oof.
哎哟。

508
00:25:20.200 --> 00:25:20.600
Oof.
哎哟。

509
00:25:20.980 --> 00:25:29.500
Now, Jenna, per Justin Spitzer, this is the only episode title that was an actual line in the script.
现在，珍娜，据贾斯汀·斯皮策所说，这是唯一一集标题直接取自剧本台词的剧集。

510
00:25:30.220 --> 00:25:30.500
Yes.
没错。

511
00:25:30.820 --> 00:25:34.940
Justin said he had originally thought they should call it insubordination.
贾斯汀说他最初想把这一集命名为“不服从”。

512
00:25:35.300 --> 00:25:35.660
Oh.
哦。

513
00:25:36.120 --> 00:25:37.980
But they settled on Did I stutter?
但他们最终决定用“我结巴了吗？”。

514
00:25:38.200 --> 00:25:39.820
Well, I like Did I stutter better.
嗯，我更喜欢“我结巴了吗？”这个标题。

515
00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:40.660
Me too.
我也是。

516
00:25:41.660 --> 00:25:50.660
Next up, we're in Michael's office and Toby is sitting with him and he's trying to tell Michael that he needs to talk with Stanley about his insubordination.
接下来，我们来到迈克尔的办公室，托比正坐在那儿，他试图告诉迈克尔，他需要和斯坦利谈谈他这种不服从的行为。

517
00:25:50.660 --> 00:25:58.560
And once again, Toby is in Michael's corner and Michael just refuses to see Toby as someone who could be there for him.
而托比再一次站在了迈克尔这边，但迈克尔就是拒绝把托比看作是一个能支持他的人。

518
00:25:59.040 --> 00:25:59.160
Yeah.
是啊。

519
00:25:59.300 --> 00:26:05.160
He tries to tell Toby that he misinterpreted what he saw, that they were actually a couple of pals.
他试图告诉托比，他误解了自己所看到的，他们其实是好哥们。

520
00:26:05.300 --> 00:26:06.500
They're kind of joshing around.
他们只是在开玩笑。

521
00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:10.900
Toby wouldn't know because Toby doesn't have friends, Michael says.
迈克尔说，托比不会懂的，因为托比根本没有朋友。

522
00:26:11.260 --> 00:26:11.460
Yeah.
是啊。

523
00:26:11.460 --> 00:26:14.860
If you had a friend, you would say something like this.
如果你有朋友，你会说这样的话：

524
00:26:15.200 --> 00:26:16.760
Hey, you're poor.
嘿，你真穷。

525
00:26:16.980 --> 00:26:18.840
Well, hey, your mom is dead.
嘿，你妈死了。

526
00:26:19.020 --> 00:26:20.060
That's what friends do.
朋友之间就是这么相处的。

527
00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:20.560
Yeah.
是啊。

528
00:26:21.020 --> 00:26:22.600
So there you go, Toby.
所以就是这样，托比。

529
00:26:22.880 --> 00:26:24.060
Get some friends.
去交点朋友吧。

530
00:26:24.060 --> 00:26:30.160
But it's clear at the end of this meeting that Michael is going to be expected to do something about what happened.
但这次会议结束时很明显，迈克尔必须得对发生的事情采取行动。

531
00:26:30.420 --> 00:26:32.840
It's also clear that Michael's really anxious about it.
同样明显的是，迈克尔对此感到非常焦虑。

532
00:26:32.940 --> 00:26:34.280
He says he has a stomach ache.
他说他胃疼。

533
00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:37.540
And Jenna, there's a deleted scene.
而且珍娜，有一个删减片段。

534
00:26:37.980 --> 00:26:39.560
It's so great.
太棒了。

535
00:26:39.800 --> 00:26:45.040
First of all, it shows the geography of Dunder Mifflin in a whole new way that we've never seen before.
首先，它以一种我们从未见过的方式展示了邓德·米夫林的地理布局。

536
00:26:45.380 --> 00:26:50.000
So in this deleted scene, there's a talking head and it's over the action.
在这个删减片段里，有一个访谈镜头，背景里正发生着动作。

537
00:26:50.180 --> 00:26:50.880
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

538
00:26:50.880 --> 00:26:54.660
And Michael is talking about how him and Stanley are friends.
迈克尔正在谈论他和斯坦利是朋友。

539
00:26:54.880 --> 00:26:57.180
In fact, Stanley is one of his oldest friends.
事实上，斯坦利是他最老的朋友之一。

540
00:26:57.380 --> 00:27:02.040
But while he's saying all this, he's walking out of his office and he clearly has to go pee.
但当他说这些话的时候，他正走出办公室，显然他急着去上厕所。

541
00:27:02.200 --> 00:27:04.720
And he sees Stanley and he pivots hard right.
他看到了斯坦利，于是猛地向右转。

542
00:27:04.960 --> 00:27:11.860
He goes out the front door of Dunder Mifflin, past the elevators to the stairwell door next to Vance Refrigeration.
他走出了邓德·米夫林的前门，经过电梯，走向万斯制冷公司旁边的楼梯间门。

543
00:27:12.020 --> 00:27:18.480
He goes down the stairs, out the front door of Dunder Mifflin, through the parking lot to a back door.
他走下楼梯，出了邓德·米夫林的前门，穿过停车场，来到一扇后门。

544
00:27:18.480 --> 00:27:21.400
That's another stairwell up those stairs.
那是另一个楼梯间，顺着那些楼梯上去。

545
00:27:21.400 --> 00:27:25.440
And he comes out by the break room, by the vending machines.
然后他从休息室旁、自动售货机旁走了出来。

546
00:27:25.520 --> 00:27:30.040
And then he walks through the annex, into the kitchen, into the men's room.
接着他穿过附楼，走进厨房，进了男厕所。

547
00:27:30.560 --> 00:27:36.420
That's what he did because he had to go pee and he did not want to walk past Stanley's desk.
他之所以这么做，是因为他急着上厕所，而且他不想经过斯坦利的办公桌。

548
00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:37.380
Wow.
哇。

549
00:27:37.380 --> 00:27:44.620
And we've never seen anyone in the run of the show come up the back stairwell into the area where the break room is.
而且在整部剧的播出过程中，我们从未见过有人从后楼梯上来，进入休息室所在的区域。

550
00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:45.620
That's right.
没错。

551
00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:47.440
I loved it just visually.
我光从视觉上就很喜欢它。

552
00:27:47.860 --> 00:27:51.680
And that shows you the extremes he was going to to avoid Stanley.
这足以说明他为了躲避斯坦利有多么不择手段。

553
00:27:52.180 --> 00:28:01.860
Well, now we're going to get into the B storyline of this episode, which is that Andy is selling his car, his Xterra, and Dwight is going to buy it.
好了，现在我们要进入这一集的B线剧情了，那就是安迪要卖掉他的车，那辆Xterra，而德怀特打算买下它。

554
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:04.640
His Xterra when he was driving a Prius.
他明明开着一辆普锐斯，却要卖掉Xterra。

555
00:28:04.780 --> 00:28:06.400
So I don't know what's happening here.
所以我也不知道这到底是怎么回事。

556
00:28:06.400 --> 00:28:07.600
I know.
我知道。

557
00:28:08.060 --> 00:28:09.260
What's that about?
那是怎么回事？

558
00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:10.440
You know what?
你知道吗？

559
00:28:10.500 --> 00:28:12.900
In my mind, it was like his old car from college.
在我看来，那就像是他大学时期的旧车。

560
00:28:13.380 --> 00:28:13.700
Hmm.
嗯。

561
00:28:14.120 --> 00:28:14.940
Maybe so.
也许吧。

562
00:28:15.180 --> 00:28:16.340
From his Cornell days.
他康奈尔大学时期的车。

563
00:28:16.840 --> 00:28:20.280
Well, we had a fan question from Barbara G and Rebecca H.
我们收到了芭芭拉·G和丽贝卡·H的粉丝提问。

564
00:28:20.480 --> 00:28:25.840
At 6 minutes 45 seconds, Dwight points out that there's a scratch on Andy's Xterra.
在6分45秒处，德怀特指出安迪的Xterra上有道划痕。

565
00:28:26.040 --> 00:28:33.460
In a deleted scene from safety training, Angela, you might remember, Angela keys Andy's car.
在《安全培训》的一段删减片段里，安吉拉——你们可能还记得——安吉拉划了安迪的车。

566
00:28:33.460 --> 00:28:36.520
Did Angela also key his Xterra?
安吉拉也划了他的Xterra吗？

567
00:28:36.900 --> 00:28:38.860
I don't think so.
我不这么认为。

568
00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:40.760
I think she just keyed the Prius.
我觉得她当时划的是那辆普锐斯。

569
00:28:41.060 --> 00:28:47.320
But in the script, you guys, Angela is watching all of this interaction between Dwight and Andy.
但在剧本里，伙计们，安吉拉一直在观察德怀特和安迪之间的所有互动。

570
00:28:47.540 --> 00:28:51.480
She is perhaps titillated by it, fascinated, curious.
她或许对此感到兴奋、着迷，充满好奇。

571
00:28:51.480 --> 00:28:58.460
But there are several scenes where she's peering through the window, the camera busts her at one point, and she gets agitated.
但有几个场景是她透过窗户窥视，摄像机有一次抓拍到了她，她显得有些焦躁。

572
00:28:58.640 --> 00:29:02.760
So she is sort of watching all of this all day long.
所以她整天都在盯着这一切看。

573
00:29:03.100 --> 00:29:11.240
Well, Dwight ends up bullying Andy into selling him the car at a very low rate, way under asking.
最终，德怀特通过霸凌手段迫使安迪以极低的价格把车卖给他，远低于要价。

574
00:29:11.780 --> 00:29:16.580
He does that thing where he's like, do it, sell it, give it to me, say yes now, say yes now.
他用了那一招，就是那种：快点，卖给我，把它给我，现在就答应，现在就答应。

575
00:29:16.660 --> 00:29:20.820
Three, two, one, five, four, three, say yes.
三，二，一，五，四，三，快答应。

576
00:29:21.720 --> 00:29:22.720
And it works.
结果奏效了。

577
00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:24.100
He says, okay.
安迪说，好吧。

578
00:29:24.640 --> 00:29:26.240
Now, here's an interesting tidbit.
现在，有个有趣的幕后花絮。

579
00:29:26.420 --> 00:29:31.680
This car, this Xterra, actually belonged to our hairdresser, Kim Ferry.
这辆车，这辆Xterra，实际上是我们发型师金·费里的。

580
00:29:31.680 --> 00:29:33.820
And she was actually selling it.
她当时确实正打算卖掉它。

581
00:29:33.960 --> 00:29:34.800
She was.
没错。

582
00:29:35.100 --> 00:29:36.180
It was so crazy.
真是太巧了。

583
00:29:36.480 --> 00:29:38.960
She let us borrow her car for this episode.
她把车借给我们拍这一集。

584
00:29:38.960 --> 00:29:40.340
And then she sold it.
然后她把它卖了。

585
00:29:40.960 --> 00:29:42.500
Just like these guys.
就像他们一样。

586
00:29:43.140 --> 00:29:49.260
Well, I guess Michael is going to finally baby step up to Stanley's desk.
好了，我想迈克尔终于要小心翼翼地走到斯坦利的办公桌前了。

587
00:29:49.440 --> 00:29:53.800
And he's basically going to forgive Stanley before Stanley has even apologized.
他基本上要在斯坦利道歉之前就先原谅他。

588
00:29:54.400 --> 00:30:00.540
But the way he approaches Stanley really reminds me of like when my kids want something, but they don't want to ask me.
但他接近斯坦利的方式真的让我想起我的孩子们想要什么东西，却又不好意思开口的时候。

589
00:30:00.540 --> 00:30:03.600
And they just come and stand by you and kind of hover.
他们就过来站在你身边，在那儿徘徊。

590
00:30:03.860 --> 00:30:04.240
Yeah.
是啊。

591
00:30:04.660 --> 00:30:06.980
He's just standing next to Stanley's desk.
他只是站在斯坦利的桌子旁边。

592
00:30:07.100 --> 00:30:09.400
And Stanley's like, yeah, what do you want?
斯坦利就说，怎么了，你想要什么？

593
00:30:10.080 --> 00:30:10.640
Yeah.
是啊。

594
00:30:10.760 --> 00:30:12.500
And he's like, you know, nothing.
他就说，你知道的，没什么。

595
00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:15.380
I think I just want to say like we're cool, right?
我想我只是想说我们没事了，对吧？

596
00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:17.040
Like I forgive you.
就像是我原谅你了。

597
00:30:17.280 --> 00:30:20.380
And we've forgotten about what happened.
我们已经忘了之前发生的事了。

598
00:30:20.820 --> 00:30:21.260
Right?
对吧？

599
00:30:21.600 --> 00:30:22.060
Yeah.
是啊。

600
00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:25.380
Now, Stanley could just say yes.
其实斯坦利本可以只说一句“好的”。

601
00:30:25.600 --> 00:30:26.240
I know.
我知道。

602
00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:27.680
But he does not.
但他不知道。

603
00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:32.500
I think Stanley has had years of putting up with Michael and he's just had it.
我觉得斯坦利忍受迈克尔已经很多年了，他现在真是受够了。

604
00:30:33.100 --> 00:30:33.280
Yeah.
没错。

605
00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:43.900
Since that didn't work, Michael is going to sit with Dwight and try to figure out, is there a way that someone else might be able to discipline Stanley?
既然那招没用，迈克尔打算和德怀特坐下来商量，看看有没有办法让别人来管教斯坦利？

606
00:30:44.180 --> 00:30:47.920
Does Stanley report to anyone else besides Michael?
除了迈克尔，斯坦利还向别人汇报工作吗？

607
00:30:47.920 --> 00:30:55.380
And this is when Dwight gets out his very extensive, very hilarious employee org chart.
这时候德怀特拿出了他那份非常详尽、非常搞笑的员工组织架构图。

608
00:30:55.660 --> 00:30:57.160
It's so elaborate.
它做得太复杂了。

609
00:30:57.160 --> 00:30:59.100
It was really well made.
真的做得很好。

610
00:30:59.420 --> 00:31:01.820
He has a like tripod.
他有个类似三脚架的东西。

611
00:31:01.820 --> 00:31:02.980
He sets it on.
他把它架在上面。

612
00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:04.800
There's like an overlay.
还有类似覆盖层的东西。

613
00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:07.680
I mean, Jenna, this thing was not cheap.
我是说，珍娜，这东西可不便宜。

614
00:31:07.680 --> 00:31:18.840
Well, Brent told us that the entire writing staff put a huge amount of time and effort into that org chart and that they had the idea that after this episode,
嗯，布伦特告诉我们，整个编剧团队在那张组织架构图上投入了大量的时间和精力，他们当时想的是，这一集播出后，

615
00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:22.460
NBC could sell the org chart as posters.
NBC可以把这张架构图印成海报来卖。

616
00:31:22.720 --> 00:31:28.640
So they filled it with all these little jokes that you can't even really spot in the episode itself.
所以他们往上面填满了各种小笑话，你在剧集里甚至都看不出来。

617
00:31:28.640 --> 00:31:35.300
And unfortunately, though, the poster did not become the runaway bestseller they had hoped it would be.
但遗憾的是，这张海报并没有像他们希望的那样成为畅销爆款。

618
00:31:35.760 --> 00:31:42.660
However, Kent Sabornak sent me a picture of it and we will put it in the pod so you can really unpack it if you'd like.
不过，肯特·萨博纳克给我发了一张照片，我们会把它放在播客里，如果你想的话，可以仔细研究一下。

619
00:31:43.160 --> 00:31:48.580
Yeah, I looked at that last night and the detail of the menstruation cycles of the women.
是啊，我昨晚看了，上面还有女性经期周期的细节。

620
00:31:49.160 --> 00:31:51.880
You know, Dwight has shared that he clocks all of that.
你知道的，德怀特曾分享过他会记录所有这些信息。

621
00:31:52.080 --> 00:31:53.020
Well, he wasn't kidding.
看来他没开玩笑。

622
00:31:53.520 --> 00:31:55.460
Angela, we got a fan question about this scene.
安吉拉，我们收到一个关于这一幕的粉丝提问。

623
00:31:55.460 --> 00:32:01.280
At 9 minutes, 34 seconds, did Rain improvise touching Michael's face with his pointer?
在9分34秒时，雷恩用教鞭触碰迈克尔的脸是即兴发挥吗？

624
00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:02.900
Yes.
是的。

625
00:32:03.680 --> 00:32:04.780
Yes, he did.
没错，他是即兴发挥的。

626
00:32:04.780 --> 00:32:06.880
And they could not get through it.
而且他们当时根本拍不下去。

627
00:32:07.060 --> 00:32:15.260
They were cracking up something so sort of delicate and intimate about Dwight touching Michael's face with that metal pointer.
他们笑得不行，德怀特用那根金属教鞭触碰迈克尔的脸，这动作有一种说不出的微妙和亲昵感。

628
00:32:15.660 --> 00:32:19.280
And those two fellas were just disintegrating into laughter.
那两个家伙当时简直笑得东倒西歪。

629
00:32:19.540 --> 00:32:20.460
It's in the bloopers.
花絮里有这段。

630
00:32:20.700 --> 00:32:21.940
It's so fun to watch.
看起来太好玩了。

631
00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:29.100
Justin said before they started the scene, they had to decide whether or not Rain would have that metal pointer or a laser pointer.
贾斯汀说在开始拍摄这一幕之前，他们得决定雷恩是用金属教鞭还是激光笔。

632
00:32:29.640 --> 00:32:31.180
And he's so glad.
他感到非常庆幸。

633
00:32:31.380 --> 00:32:34.060
I'm so glad they gave him the metal pointer.
我也很庆幸他们给了他金属教鞭。

634
00:32:34.440 --> 00:32:34.580
Yeah.
没错。

635
00:32:35.280 --> 00:32:40.340
Brent said that after Rain improvised it once, they loved it and they had him do it again.
布伦特说雷恩即兴发挥了一次之后，他们非常喜欢，就让他又做了一次。

636
00:32:40.340 --> 00:32:46.100
And it took over seven takes before they got even three seconds of usable footage.
他们拍了七次以上才勉强凑出三秒钟能用的镜头。

637
00:32:46.240 --> 00:32:50.020
And that's what you see in the episode was like take number eight.
你在剧里看到的已经是第八次拍摄的成果了。

638
00:32:50.640 --> 00:32:54.160
Well, back at reception, Kevin is complimenting Pam's glasses.
回到前台，凯文正在夸奖帕姆的眼镜。

639
00:32:54.420 --> 00:32:56.080
I mean, they're kind of a turn on for him.
我是说，这对他来说有点诱人。

640
00:32:56.980 --> 00:32:59.080
Jenna, there's a lot more in the script.
珍娜，剧本里还有更多内容。

641
00:32:59.440 --> 00:33:02.340
In fact, Kevin says you're basically in his league now.
事实上，凯文说你现在基本上和他是一个档次了。

642
00:33:03.460 --> 00:33:05.980
So I think there were a few alts for this scene.
所以我认为这一幕还有几个备选方案。

643
00:33:06.180 --> 00:33:07.680
I remember shooting it.
我记得当时拍摄的情景。

644
00:33:07.840 --> 00:33:09.420
We were laughing so hard.
我们当时笑得太厉害了。

645
00:33:09.640 --> 00:33:14.220
There's also that famous line where he says, can you say these are due back Thursday?
还有那句名台词，他说，你能说这些书周四要还吗？

646
00:33:14.720 --> 00:33:16.720
And Pam's like, no, no.
帕姆说，不，不行。

647
00:33:17.380 --> 00:33:22.480
At nine minutes, 58 seconds at the very top of this interaction between Pam and Kevin,
在9分58秒，也就是帕姆和凯文这段互动的最开始，

648
00:33:22.820 --> 00:33:27.160
I want you to know that John is actively playing free cell on his computer.
我想让你知道，约翰当时正在电脑上玩空当接龙。

649
00:33:27.420 --> 00:33:28.420
Oh, I saw it.
哦，我看到了。

650
00:33:28.540 --> 00:33:29.900
It's not just on his computer.
那可不只是在他的电脑上。

651
00:33:30.100 --> 00:33:31.620
You can see him moving the car.
你可以看到他在挪动那辆车。

652
00:33:31.620 --> 00:33:33.520
Oh, no, he's full on playing.
噢，不，他完全是在玩真的。

653
00:33:34.260 --> 00:33:40.060
But this interaction between Kevin and Pam is going to cause Pam to take her glasses off now
但凯文和帕姆之间的这次互动，导致帕姆现在要把眼镜摘下来了，

654
00:33:40.060 --> 00:33:40.980
for the rest of the day.
接下来的这一整天都不戴了。

655
00:33:41.140 --> 00:33:41.680
She's done.
她受够了。

656
00:33:41.920 --> 00:33:42.960
She's sick of the comments.
她厌倦了那些评论。

657
00:33:43.280 --> 00:33:45.040
She's just going to not see.
她干脆选择看不见。

658
00:33:45.520 --> 00:33:48.260
But how bad is this woman's vision?
但这女人的视力到底有多差？

659
00:33:48.260 --> 00:33:53.180
Because she takes her glasses off and then Jenna, the phone rings and she has a hard time
因为她摘下眼镜后，珍娜，电话响了，她却很难

660
00:33:53.180 --> 00:33:54.980
finding the handle of the phone.
找到电话的话筒。

661
00:33:55.220 --> 00:33:58.640
There is a talking head that did not make it in the episode.
有一个没被剪进正片的采访镜头。

662
00:33:58.820 --> 00:33:59.420
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

663
00:33:59.420 --> 00:34:04.040
Where Pam says that her vision is 20 slash 400.
帕姆在里面说她的视力是20/400。

664
00:34:04.460 --> 00:34:10.160
I'll have you know, Angela, legal blindness is anything that's 20 slash 200 or worse.
安吉拉，我得告诉你，法律意义上的盲人是指视力在20/200或更差的人。

665
00:34:10.420 --> 00:34:15.260
So Pam would be considered legally blind without her glasses or contacts.
所以帕姆如果不戴眼镜或隐形眼镜，会被视为法律意义上的盲人。

666
00:34:15.260 --> 00:34:23.140
And basically what it means is that Pam can see things 20 feet away, but normal people could
基本上这意味着帕姆在20英尺外能看到的东西，正常人可以在

667
00:34:23.140 --> 00:34:25.700
see that same thing 400 feet away.
400英尺外看到同样的东西。

668
00:34:25.880 --> 00:34:29.920
So it doesn't really track that Pam can't see the phone.
所以帕姆看不见电话这个设定其实不太合理。

669
00:34:29.920 --> 00:34:30.460
Okay.
好吧。

670
00:34:31.040 --> 00:34:35.160
What it should mean is that she can't see Stanley anymore.
这应该意味着她连斯坦利都看不清了才对。

671
00:34:35.340 --> 00:34:35.580
Okay.
好吧。

672
00:34:36.200 --> 00:34:36.400
Yeah.
是啊。

673
00:34:37.140 --> 00:34:41.520
So maybe we didn't research her eyesight properly.
所以也许我们对她视力的研究不够充分。

674
00:34:42.040 --> 00:34:46.820
But in general, though, all of her vision would be fairly blurry.
但总的来说，她的视野应该会相当模糊。

675
00:34:47.060 --> 00:34:48.560
I do remember researching that.
我记得我确实研究过这个。

676
00:34:48.560 --> 00:34:53.460
Well, I thought you played it so well, Jenna, because that's not an easy thing to play.
嗯，我觉得你演得非常好，珍娜，因为这并不是一个容易演的角色。

677
00:34:53.700 --> 00:34:57.380
And the physicality of your comedy in this episode is fantastic.
而且你这一集里的肢体喜剧表现太棒了。

678
00:34:58.000 --> 00:34:59.460
Well, thank you very much.
嗯，非常感谢。

679
00:34:59.720 --> 00:35:00.020
Yes.
是的。

680
00:35:00.720 --> 00:35:05.520
Well, guys, Michael's going to go down to the warehouse and try to get maybe some advice
好了，各位，迈克尔打算去仓库，想看看能不能得到一些建议，

681
00:35:05.520 --> 00:35:06.960
on how to deal with Stanley.
关于如何对付斯坦利。

682
00:35:06.960 --> 00:35:09.860
But before we go there, let's take a break.
但在我们去那儿之前，先休息一下。

683
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:13.900
And then we'll come back to learn a little bit about Fluffy Fingers.
回来之后，我们会了解一点关于“毛茸茸的手指”的事。

684
00:35:25.140 --> 00:35:26.480
Okay, guys, we're back.
好了，各位，我们回来了。

685
00:35:26.600 --> 00:35:30.960
And as promised, we're going to break down this scene between Michael and Daryl.
正如承诺的那样，我们要来剖析迈克尔和达里尔之间的这场戏。

686
00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:32.440
It's amazing.
太精彩了。

687
00:35:32.840 --> 00:35:34.360
Everything about it is amazing.
关于它的一切都很精彩。

688
00:35:34.500 --> 00:35:39.300
Even just from a technical standpoint, this was such a tiny, tiny room.
即使单从技术角度来看，这间屋子也实在太小太小了。

689
00:35:39.480 --> 00:35:44.640
And Randall had to shoot through the door in a window and capture this moment.
兰德尔必须透过门上的窗户拍摄，捕捉这一刻。

690
00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:45.960
It's so beautifully done.
拍得太美了。

691
00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:51.200
And Michael's going to ask Daryl, hey, man, have you ever been in a gang?
迈克尔问达里尔，嘿，伙计，你有没有混过帮派？

692
00:35:51.740 --> 00:35:56.660
And Daryl needs to know what Michael needs to say.
而达里尔需要知道迈克尔想听什么。

693
00:35:56.880 --> 00:35:57.220
Yeah.
是啊。

694
00:35:57.340 --> 00:36:02.380
So he says he has been in not just one gang, but several.
所以他说他不仅混过一个帮派，而是好几个。

695
00:36:02.900 --> 00:36:03.140
Yeah.
是啊。

696
00:36:03.360 --> 00:36:08.620
He has been in the Crips and the Bloods and the Warriors and the Newsies.
他说他混过瘸帮、血帮、勇士帮，还有报童帮。

697
00:36:08.960 --> 00:36:10.540
And the Newsies on Broadway.
还有百老汇的报童帮。

698
00:36:12.180 --> 00:36:15.080
And Michael is just like, oh, my God.
迈克尔当时就震惊了，天哪。

699
00:36:15.380 --> 00:36:15.740
Yeah.
是啊。

700
00:36:16.530 --> 00:36:17.640
Oh, my God.
天哪。

701
00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:24.820
And Michael can't believe that Daryl is now about to share with him his, like, deep gang knowledge.
迈克尔简直不敢相信，达里尔现在竟然要跟他分享那些所谓的帮派深层内幕。

702
00:36:25.680 --> 00:36:25.940
Yeah.
是啊。

703
00:36:26.140 --> 00:36:29.460
What do you do if you're disrespected in the gang?
如果在帮派里被人冒犯了该怎么办？

704
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.340
Daryl's going to tell him they do something called Fluffy Fingers.
达里尔告诉他，他们会用一种叫“挠痒痒”的方法。

705
00:36:33.340 --> 00:36:38.280
And that is where you surprise the person by tickling them.
就是趁对方不注意去挠他们痒痒。

706
00:36:38.480 --> 00:36:38.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

707
00:36:39.480 --> 00:36:43.800
And you keep tickling them until they start to tickle you.
然后一直挠，直到对方也开始挠你。

708
00:36:44.280 --> 00:36:45.980
And then you're just tickling each other.
接着你们就互相挠痒痒。

709
00:36:46.240 --> 00:36:46.600
Yeah.
没错。

710
00:36:46.600 --> 00:36:47.880
And then you're over it.
然后这事儿就过去了。

711
00:36:48.160 --> 00:36:49.980
It's really effective, he says.
他说这招特别管用。

712
00:36:50.200 --> 00:36:51.820
And Michael's like, wow.
迈克尔听完觉得，哇。

713
00:36:52.200 --> 00:36:57.660
I didn't think that's how it went in the gangs.
我没想到帮派里竟然是这么处理问题的。

714
00:36:57.820 --> 00:36:58.360
But okay.
不过好吧。

715
00:36:58.880 --> 00:36:59.440
Okay.
好吧。

716
00:36:59.440 --> 00:37:00.700
Hey, Michael's like, all right.
嘿，迈克尔心想，行吧。

717
00:37:00.700 --> 00:37:03.080
I guess I should try this.
我想我应该试试这个。

718
00:37:03.080 --> 00:37:04.160
It's so great.
这太棒了。

719
00:37:04.160 --> 00:37:06.940
And both Steve and Craig play it perfectly.
史蒂夫和克雷格都演得太完美了。

720
00:37:07.380 --> 00:37:07.960
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

721
00:37:08.500 --> 00:37:13.060
Well, you know, Jenna, there was a deleted scene where Michael tries to get up the courage
珍娜，你知道吗，有个删减片段是迈克尔试图鼓起勇气

722
00:37:13.060 --> 00:37:16.260
to tickle Stanley to do the Fluffy Fingers.
去挠斯坦利痒痒，用那个“挠痒痒”大法。

723
00:37:16.500 --> 00:37:17.380
It's insane.
太疯狂了。

724
00:37:17.880 --> 00:37:19.960
Stanley is at the supply cabinet.
斯坦利当时正在储物柜那边。

725
00:37:20.220 --> 00:37:22.140
He's kind of reaching up to grab something.
他正伸手去拿东西。

726
00:37:22.380 --> 00:37:24.040
And Michael sneaks up behind him.
迈克尔悄悄溜到他身后。

727
00:37:24.100 --> 00:37:26.920
And he holds his hands up like he's going to tickle him.
他举起双手，摆出要挠他痒痒的架势。

728
00:37:27.160 --> 00:37:29.880
But then he just can't quite figure out how to do it.
但后来他实在不知道该怎么下手。

729
00:37:29.980 --> 00:37:31.340
And Stanley doesn't even notice.
而斯坦利根本没察觉到。

730
00:37:31.500 --> 00:37:32.540
And Michael backs away.
于是迈克尔又退了回去。

731
00:37:32.540 --> 00:37:37.140
And then Michael has a deleted talking head where he says, it's not Daryl's fault.
后来迈克尔还有一个删减的采访镜头，他说，这不怪达里尔。

732
00:37:37.340 --> 00:37:39.260
It was a great idea.
这是个好主意。

733
00:37:39.580 --> 00:37:42.220
I just couldn't quite figure out how to do it.
只是我实在没搞明白该怎么操作。

734
00:37:42.300 --> 00:37:42.800
I don't know.
我不知道。

735
00:37:43.000 --> 00:37:44.060
I've tried everything.
我什么都试过了。

736
00:37:44.360 --> 00:37:45.940
I'm running out of options.
我快没招了。

737
00:37:46.520 --> 00:37:47.080
Yeah.
是啊。

738
00:37:47.340 --> 00:37:51.600
And when you run out of options, you decide to fake fire someone.
当你没招的时候，你就会决定假装开除某个人。

739
00:37:51.960 --> 00:37:53.980
That's what Michael does.
这就是迈克尔干的事。

740
00:37:54.640 --> 00:37:55.700
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

741
00:37:56.280 --> 00:37:58.940
So now Ryan has arrived.
现在瑞安到了。

742
00:37:58.940 --> 00:38:01.180
He pulls up in his convertible.
他开着敞篷车过来了。

743
00:38:01.180 --> 00:38:02.640
His shirt is open.
衬衫领口敞开着。

744
00:38:03.060 --> 00:38:05.520
He winks at himself in the rearview mirror.
他对着后视镜里的自己眨了眨眼。

745
00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:06.500
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

746
00:38:06.580 --> 00:38:07.760
He's feeling real good.
他感觉好极了。

747
00:38:08.120 --> 00:38:11.380
And there was a deleted scene, Jenna, that was so good.
珍娜，还有一个删减片段特别精彩。

748
00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:12.520
He comes in the office.
他走进办公室。

749
00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:13.840
He's got bagels.
他带了百吉饼。

750
00:38:14.000 --> 00:38:15.900
But Pam doesn't have her glasses on.
但帕姆没戴眼镜。

751
00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:17.620
He tosses a bagel at her.
他把一个贝果扔向她。

752
00:38:17.820 --> 00:38:18.920
She can't see it.
她没看见。

753
00:38:19.020 --> 00:38:20.160
It hits her in the face.
贝果砸在了她脸上。

754
00:38:20.680 --> 00:38:25.060
And then he goes on, Jenna, to show Pam how to eat a bagel.
然后他接着向帕姆演示怎么吃贝果。

755
00:38:25.200 --> 00:38:30.280
He just, with his own hands, starts digging out all the good part of the bagel,
他直接用手把贝果里好吃的部分全掏了出来，

756
00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:31.200
all the middle part.
把中间部分全掏空了。

757
00:38:31.320 --> 00:38:35.140
And he says, yeah, you just eat that outer part, you know, so you don't gain weight.
他说，对，你就吃外圈就行，这样就不会长胖。

758
00:38:35.140 --> 00:38:36.700
And he kind of points to Pam's belly.
他还指了指帕姆的肚子。

759
00:38:37.260 --> 00:38:37.460
Yeah.
没错。

760
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:42.240
And I felt like that whole scene showed his state of mind, how manic he is,
我觉得整场戏展现了他的精神状态，他有多狂躁，

761
00:38:42.380 --> 00:38:44.080
throwing the bagels, digging them apart.
扔贝果，把贝果掏得乱七八糟。

762
00:38:44.180 --> 00:38:45.620
Like, oh, my gosh.
天哪，真是。

763
00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:47.300
I remember shooting that.
我记得拍那场戏的时候。

764
00:38:47.460 --> 00:38:49.580
I was sad it didn't make it in because that was really fun.
没能剪进正片里我挺难过的，因为那场戏真的很有趣。

765
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.300
You were so good in it.
你在那场戏里演得太棒了。

766
00:38:51.300 --> 00:38:53.620
I mean, he's like, he tosses a bagel at you.
我是说，他当时把贝果扔向你。

767
00:38:53.740 --> 00:38:56.220
And Jenna, I really believed you didn't see it.
而且珍娜，我真的相信你当时没看见。

768
00:38:57.200 --> 00:38:59.020
That's how good you are in the scene.
你在这场戏里的演技就是这么好。

769
00:38:59.860 --> 00:39:01.560
Anyway, so Ryan is here.
总之，瑞安在那儿。

770
00:39:01.640 --> 00:39:03.120
He's actually got some big business.
他其实是有什么大生意要谈。

771
00:39:03.180 --> 00:39:06.660
He goes in the conference room and he calls Jim in.
他走进会议室，把吉姆叫了进去。

772
00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:11.920
Toby's there and he's going to give him a formal warning about his job performance.
托比也在，他要就吉姆的工作表现对他进行正式警告。

773
00:39:12.240 --> 00:39:14.860
But the way he calls him in is so amazing.
但他叫吉姆进去的方式简直绝了。

774
00:39:15.100 --> 00:39:19.680
He's like, hey, Jim, Jim, I got to ask you a question as a true Eagles fan.
他说，嘿，吉姆，吉姆，作为真正的老鹰队球迷，我得问你个问题。

775
00:39:19.680 --> 00:39:21.160
Oh, so slimy.
噢，太油腻了。

776
00:39:21.540 --> 00:39:24.580
I thought BJ was so good in this scene.
我觉得BJ在这场戏里演得太好了。

777
00:39:24.760 --> 00:39:27.940
He was like every douchebag I've ever had a meeting with.
他演出了我见过的所有混蛋那种感觉。

778
00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:32.880
I actually recorded it off my computer and I texted it to him.
我甚至专门录下来发短信给了他。

779
00:39:33.060 --> 00:39:36.300
And I said, BJ, we're watching Did I Stutter?
我说，BJ，我们正在看《我结巴了吗？》这一集。

780
00:39:36.480 --> 00:39:40.060
And you are so brilliant and amazing in the scene.
你在戏里表现得太出色、太惊艳了。

781
00:39:40.260 --> 00:39:43.220
I just needed you to watch it so you can see how good you are.
我就是想让你看看，让你知道自己演得有多好。

782
00:39:44.340 --> 00:39:49.020
And he wrote me back and he was like, Jenna, oh, my God, I forgot about that scene.
他回我说，珍娜，天哪，我都忘了那场戏了。

783
00:39:49.020 --> 00:39:50.340
Thank you for sending this to me.
谢谢你发给我。

784
00:39:50.440 --> 00:39:51.560
That was so fun to watch.
看这段真的太有意思了。

785
00:39:51.740 --> 00:39:54.360
But that happens when we are rewatching this show.
但重温这部剧时经常会这样。

786
00:39:54.740 --> 00:40:00.900
Sometimes I will see one of our friends perform just like madness level amazing.
有时我会看到我们的朋友演得简直好到疯狂。

787
00:40:01.340 --> 00:40:02.660
And I just send it to him.
然后我就会发给他。

788
00:40:02.840 --> 00:40:06.600
I'm like, you need to be reminded of what an amazing comedic actor you are.
我会说，你需要被提醒一下你是一位多么出色的喜剧演员。

789
00:40:06.780 --> 00:40:07.420
You're welcome.
不客气。

790
00:40:07.720 --> 00:40:08.440
Oh, for sure.
那当然。

791
00:40:08.440 --> 00:40:13.220
I had a whole text thread with Phyllis because I was like, Phyllis, you are so amazing.
我之前还和菲利斯发过一长串短信，因为我说，菲利斯，你太棒了。

792
00:40:13.400 --> 00:40:14.760
Back in Yankee Swap.
在《洋基交换礼物》那集里。

793
00:40:15.020 --> 00:40:16.060
She's so good.
她演得太好了。

794
00:40:16.060 --> 00:40:16.940
I know.
我知道。

795
00:40:17.640 --> 00:40:18.740
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

796
00:40:18.960 --> 00:40:20.560
BJ is so good in these moments.
BJ在这些时刻表现得太好了。

797
00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:24.100
And Jim is like, is this because I talked to David Wallace?
吉姆问，这是因为我和大卫·华莱士谈过吗？

798
00:40:24.540 --> 00:40:25.960
And Ryan's like, no, no, no.
瑞安说，不，不，不。

799
00:40:26.120 --> 00:40:28.800
I appreciate, you know, constructive criticism.
我很感激建设性的批评，你知道的。

800
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:30.040
I thrive on it.
我靠这个进步。

801
00:40:30.220 --> 00:40:30.400
Yeah.
是啊。

802
00:40:30.620 --> 00:40:31.540
So douchey.
真够混蛋的。

803
00:40:31.920 --> 00:40:34.440
And he says you can get more details from Toby.
他说你可以从托比那里得到更多细节。

804
00:40:34.840 --> 00:40:36.660
This leads to a Toby talking head.
这引出了托比的单人采访。

805
00:40:36.840 --> 00:40:39.200
And dare I say that Toby seems smug?
我敢说托比看起来很自鸣得意吗？

806
00:40:39.580 --> 00:40:40.740
Oh, for sure.
哦，绝对是。

807
00:40:41.320 --> 00:40:41.580
Yeah.
是啊。

808
00:40:41.900 --> 00:40:47.100
Toby says, I'd say all the goofing around at Pam's desk and hanging out with Pam has finally caught up with him.
托比说，我会说在帕姆桌边胡闹以及和帕姆混在一起，终于让他自食其果了。

809
00:40:47.640 --> 00:40:49.720
Fans were furious, Jenna.
粉丝们很愤怒，珍娜。

810
00:40:50.100 --> 00:40:53.700
When this episode came out, they hated Toby so much.
这一集播出时，他们非常讨厌托比。

811
00:40:53.840 --> 00:40:57.460
I mean, in the episode before, he put his hand on Pam's knee.
我是说，在上一集里，他把手放在了帕姆的膝盖上。

812
00:40:57.720 --> 00:40:58.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

813
00:40:58.380 --> 00:41:03.120
And now it seems like he's going behind Jim's back to try to get him fired.
现在看起来他好像在背后搞小动作，想让吉姆被解雇。

814
00:41:03.480 --> 00:41:03.880
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

815
00:41:04.420 --> 00:41:11.480
And Jenna, if you thought you hated Toby with that talking head, had you seen the deleted scene between Jim and Toby?
珍娜，如果你觉得那个单人采访让你讨厌托比的话，你有没有看过吉姆和托比之间那段被删掉的戏？

816
00:41:11.780 --> 00:41:14.620
And then Ryan, you would have been like, oh, my God.
如果是那样的话，瑞安，你当时肯定会觉得，天哪。

817
00:41:14.780 --> 00:41:17.680
People would have, Toby would not have been able to come back from it.
人们会觉得，托比根本没法从那件事里翻身了。

818
00:41:17.840 --> 00:41:19.420
Sam, can you play that deleted scene?
山姆，你能播放那段被删掉的戏吗？

819
00:41:20.080 --> 00:41:21.100
A formal warning.
正式警告。

820
00:41:21.380 --> 00:41:21.600
Seriously.
说真的。

821
00:41:22.220 --> 00:41:26.440
Well, as you know, Dwight has filed a lot of complaints against you over the years.
嗯，如你所知，多年来德怀特对你投诉了很多次。

822
00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:27.280
And no one cared.
但没人理会。

823
00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:30.640
But now it's being looked at as more of a productivity issue.
可现在这件事被视为一个生产力问题。

824
00:41:31.420 --> 00:41:31.900
Productivity?
生产力？

825
00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:32.800
My numbers are good.
我的业绩很好。

826
00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:33.840
I know.
我知道。

827
00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:38.140
But Ryan thinks that they're not good enough.
但瑞安认为还不够好。

828
00:41:39.180 --> 00:41:40.060
Wallace likes Jim.
华莱士喜欢吉姆。

829
00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:43.080
So going after him, that's a risky move for me.
所以针对他，对我来说是个冒险的举动。

830
00:41:43.480 --> 00:41:46.000
But in business, you've got to take risks.
但在商场上，你必须冒险。

831
00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:50.120
Sometimes you've got to get out on the open highway with a top down.
有时候你得开着敞篷车行驶在开阔的高速公路上。

832
00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:56.440
Oh, my God.
天哪。

833
00:41:56.860 --> 00:42:00.340
And Ryan is trying to put the top down to his car and it won't go down.
瑞安正试图把他的车顶篷放下来，但放不下来。

834
00:42:01.840 --> 00:42:02.360
Wow.
哇。

835
00:42:02.820 --> 00:42:05.500
But, yeah, can you imagine if those scenes have been left in?
但是，天哪，你能想象如果那些戏份被保留下来会怎样吗？

836
00:42:06.260 --> 00:42:16.160
Oh, well, Angela, speaking of treachery, Dwight has washed the Xterra and he's now reselling it for over $9,000.
哦，对了，安吉拉，说到背叛，德怀特洗了那辆Xterra，现在正以超过9000美元的价格转卖。

837
00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:18.560
He's selling it for a profit.
他在靠这个赚钱。

838
00:42:18.960 --> 00:42:21.460
Oh, and Andy is like, what the hell, man?
哦，安迪当时就像是，搞什么鬼，伙计？

839
00:42:22.360 --> 00:42:23.320
Angela's impressed.
安吉拉印象深刻。

840
00:42:24.080 --> 00:42:25.260
Angela's like, oh, yeah.
安吉拉就像是，哦，太棒了。

841
00:42:25.680 --> 00:42:26.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

842
00:42:26.560 --> 00:42:27.280
You got him.
你赢了他。

843
00:42:27.380 --> 00:42:28.000
You're smarter.
你更聪明。

844
00:42:28.460 --> 00:42:30.580
She loves two men dueling over her.
她喜欢看两个男人为她争斗。

845
00:42:30.860 --> 00:42:31.840
She really does.
她确实喜欢。

846
00:42:32.040 --> 00:42:32.400
I know.
我知道。

847
00:42:32.880 --> 00:42:35.600
You guys remember, Michael has run out of options.
你们还记得吗，迈克尔已经别无选择了。

848
00:42:35.860 --> 00:42:37.580
Fluffy fingers isn't going to work for him.
“毛茸茸的手指”那招对他不管用了。

849
00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:40.940
So he's going to have to do the thing he didn't want to do.
所以他不得不去做他不想做的事。

850
00:42:41.200 --> 00:42:44.700
He's going to have to fake fire Stanley to teach him a lesson.
他不得不假装解雇斯坦利来给他一个教训。

851
00:42:44.700 --> 00:42:48.480
And he comes out of his office and he announces it to everyone.
然后他走出办公室，向大家宣布了这件事。

852
00:42:48.660 --> 00:42:55.020
He says, guys, guys, guys, listen, I'm going to fake fire Stanley, but I just want you to react as if I'm really firing Stanley.
他说，伙计们，听着，我要假装解雇斯坦利，但我希望你们表现得就像我真的在解雇他一样。

853
00:42:55.280 --> 00:43:00.840
And everybody's like, if you hadn't told us what you were doing, we would have reacted correctly.
大家心想，如果你没告诉我们你要做什么，我们本来就会做出正确的反应。

854
00:43:01.440 --> 00:43:04.400
And he's like, oh, my gosh, why aren't you understanding this?
他却说，天哪，你们为什么就是不明白呢？

855
00:43:04.400 --> 00:43:08.780
The person that says it, the person that's the voice of reason is Kevin.
说出这句话的人，那个理智的声音，是凯文。

856
00:43:09.440 --> 00:43:10.420
I know.
我知道。

857
00:43:10.740 --> 00:43:14.360
You know you're in trouble when Kevin is the voice of reason.
当凯文都成了理智的化身时，你就知道麻烦大了。

858
00:43:14.920 --> 00:43:18.780
Stanley walks into the bullpen and Michael fake fires him.
斯坦利走进办公区，迈克尔假装解雇了他。

859
00:43:18.940 --> 00:43:21.140
And it does not go well.
结果并不顺利。

860
00:43:21.360 --> 00:43:23.960
Stanley unleashes on him.
斯坦利对他大发雷霆。

861
00:43:24.140 --> 00:43:27.600
Just a tirade of insults.
简直是一连串的辱骂。

862
00:43:27.840 --> 00:43:31.800
I remember when we filmed this, Jenna, and you could have heard a pin drop.
珍娜，我记得我们拍这一段的时候，现场安静得连根针掉在地上都能听见。

863
00:43:32.200 --> 00:43:32.700
Yes.
没错。

864
00:43:32.700 --> 00:43:36.480
It was such a beautifully dramatic moment.
那是一个非常精彩的戏剧性时刻。

865
00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:39.660
Leslie crushed it.
莱斯利演得太棒了。

866
00:43:39.940 --> 00:43:44.380
Yeah, you guys, we reached out to Leslie because we really,
是啊，大家，我们联系了莱斯利，因为我们真的，

867
00:43:44.640 --> 00:43:52.660
really wanted him to come on the pod today because this is just a tour de force storyline and performance by him in this episode.
真的非常希望他今天能来参加播客，因为他在这一集里的表演和剧情简直是巅峰之作。

868
00:43:52.920 --> 00:43:55.740
And he is filming this week.
但他这周在拍戏。

869
00:43:55.920 --> 00:43:59.220
He is filming something and he couldn't come on.
他在拍别的东西，所以没能过来。

870
00:43:59.220 --> 00:44:02.740
But he did want us to share with you that this monologue was completely scripted.
但他确实想让我们告诉大家，这段独白是完全照着剧本演的。

871
00:44:02.900 --> 00:44:04.020
This was not improvised.
这不是即兴发挥。

872
00:44:04.240 --> 00:44:11.760
You know, and I remember, Angela, that he worked on this and he delivered it like it was just an amazing performance.
安吉拉，我记得他为了这段戏下了很大功夫，呈现出的表演令人惊叹。

873
00:44:11.760 --> 00:44:13.300
And he nailed it every take.
每一条他都演得完美无缺。

874
00:44:13.460 --> 00:44:14.060
Every take.
每一条都是。

875
00:44:14.060 --> 00:44:16.160
He was 100% off book.
他完全背下了台词。

876
00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:18.300
He showed up ready to throw it down.
他做好了全力以赴的准备。

877
00:44:18.560 --> 00:44:22.420
And we were just all so happy for him.
我们都为他感到高兴。

878
00:44:22.780 --> 00:44:24.100
This moment was amazing.
这一刻太精彩了。

879
00:44:24.100 --> 00:44:26.740
And I remember us all applauding at the end of the scene.
我记得在那场戏结束时，我们所有人都为他鼓掌。

880
00:44:26.940 --> 00:44:27.340
Yeah.
没错。

881
00:44:27.520 --> 00:44:29.160
Well, Michael throws everybody out.
好吧，迈克尔把所有人都赶了出去。

882
00:44:29.920 --> 00:44:32.220
He yells and says, everybody get out.
他大喊着说，所有人都出去。

883
00:44:32.420 --> 00:44:32.800
Everybody.
所有人。

884
00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:33.620
Except Stanley.
除了斯坦利。

885
00:44:33.880 --> 00:44:34.500
Everybody out.
都出去。

886
00:44:34.720 --> 00:44:36.840
And everyone gets the hell out.
于是大家全都滚蛋了。

887
00:44:37.040 --> 00:44:47.260
And Jenna, in the script, which isn't in the deleted scenes, but in the script, Michael turns to the cameras and says, you two cameras out of here.
珍娜，在剧本里——虽然删减片段里没有——迈克尔转向摄像机说，你们两台摄像机也给我出去。

888
00:44:47.500 --> 00:44:48.020
Everybody.
所有人。

889
00:44:48.740 --> 00:44:49.060
Wow.
哇。

890
00:44:49.360 --> 00:44:55.600
And that's why at 18 minutes, 17 seconds, you see the cameras sneak back in.
这就是为什么在18分17秒时，你会看到摄像机又偷偷溜了回来。

891
00:44:55.740 --> 00:44:58.820
It's because in the script, Michael told them to get out.
因为在剧本里，迈克尔确实让他们出去了。

892
00:44:59.320 --> 00:45:00.580
I loved that move.
我喜欢这个设计。

893
00:45:01.020 --> 00:45:09.240
I loved it because when Michael is alone with Stanley or thinks he's alone with Stanley, he gets really vulnerable.
我喜欢它是因为当迈克尔和斯坦利单独相处，或者以为只有他们两人时，他会变得非常脆弱。

894
00:45:09.480 --> 00:45:10.800
There's tears in his eyes.
他眼里含着泪水。

895
00:45:10.800 --> 00:45:13.640
And he says, why do you pick on me?
他说，你为什么要针对我？

896
00:45:13.940 --> 00:45:16.200
Like, why do you pick on me like this?
就是说，你为什么要这样针对我？

897
00:45:16.360 --> 00:45:17.740
And it's really vulnerable.
那一刻真的很脆弱。

898
00:45:18.560 --> 00:45:21.980
And Stanley, very matter-of-factly, says, I don't respect you.
而斯坦利非常客观地回答说，我不尊重你。

899
00:45:22.600 --> 00:45:31.360
And then I felt like Michael had such an honest moment that could not have happened if the cameras were there, where he says, fine, I accept that.
然后我觉得迈克尔有了一个非常坦诚的时刻，如果摄像机在场的话，这一幕是不可能发生的，他说，好吧，我接受。

900
00:45:31.620 --> 00:45:32.700
You don't respect me.
你不尊重我。

901
00:45:32.820 --> 00:45:33.960
I accept it.
我接受。

902
00:45:34.040 --> 00:45:37.320
But you can't talk to me like that here.
但你不能在这里那样跟我说话。

903
00:45:37.760 --> 00:45:39.180
I am your boss.
我是你的上司。

904
00:45:39.360 --> 00:45:41.180
And it just cannot be done.
而且这根本行不通。

905
00:45:41.180 --> 00:45:43.240
And I agree with you, Angela.
安吉拉，我同意你的看法。

906
00:45:43.600 --> 00:45:50.560
Anytime Michael knows the cameras are there, he can't help but perform in some way for them.
迈克尔只要知道摄像机在场，就忍不住要在那儿表演一番。

907
00:45:51.110 --> 00:45:57.860
And so I feel like we're seeing a side of Michael Scott that can only be seen when he doesn't know the cameras are there.
所以我感觉我们看到了迈克尔·斯科特只有在不知道摄像机在场时才会展现的一面。

908
00:45:58.540 --> 00:45:58.680
Yeah.
没错。

909
00:45:58.680 --> 00:46:06.200
And that was such a fun part of our show, playing with who are our characters when we know the cameras are there and when we don't.
这正是我们剧集里非常有趣的一部分，即探讨角色在知道和不知道摄像机在场时会有什么不同。

910
00:46:06.340 --> 00:46:11.600
And I loved that we got to reveal these little different parts of ourselves in these different ways.
我喜欢我们能以这种方式展现出角色身上那些细微的不同侧面。

911
00:46:12.100 --> 00:46:12.960
Oh, me too.
哦，我也是。

912
00:46:13.120 --> 00:46:15.120
It made the show so rich, right?
这让剧集内容变得非常丰富，对吧？

913
00:46:15.400 --> 00:46:16.040
It's cool.
这很酷。

914
00:46:16.220 --> 00:46:16.960
And you know what?
你知道吗？

915
00:46:17.080 --> 00:46:18.480
They have this moment of resolution.
他们达成了和解。

916
00:46:18.880 --> 00:46:19.740
They're like, fine.
他们就像是说，好吧。

917
00:46:19.740 --> 00:46:22.180
We now know our rules of engagement, right?
我们现在知道彼此的相处规则了，对吧？

918
00:46:22.180 --> 00:46:23.640
Yeah, they shake hands.
是的，他们握手言和了。

919
00:46:24.140 --> 00:46:24.280
Done.
搞定。

920
00:46:24.560 --> 00:46:27.260
This leads to Michael having a talking head.
这引出了迈克尔的一段采访镜头。

921
00:46:27.400 --> 00:46:32.520
He's really stuck on the idea of respect, getting no respect.
他真的纠结于“尊重”这个概念，觉得没人尊重他。

922
00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:36.620
And this just sends his brain into Rodney Dangerfield land.
这让他的大脑直接进入了罗德尼·丹格菲尔德的频道。

923
00:46:36.920 --> 00:46:43.180
So he's going to do some real kind of like off-the-cuff Rodney Dangerfield impressions,
所以他开始做一些即兴的罗德尼·丹格菲尔德模仿秀，

924
00:46:43.180 --> 00:46:51.220
which morphs into a Jeff Foxworthy impression and then Borat and then Jerry Seinfeld and then back to Rodney Dangerfield again.
接着又变成了杰夫·福克斯沃西，然后是波拉特，再然后是杰瑞·宋飞，最后又回到了罗德尼·丹格菲尔德。

925
00:46:51.220 --> 00:46:53.360
And it's a pretty epic talking head.
那真是一段史诗级的采访镜头。

926
00:46:53.660 --> 00:46:54.600
It is.
确实。

927
00:46:54.780 --> 00:47:02.020
Well, you know, Jenna, that talking head, that whole Rodney Dangerfield comic riff is not in the shooting draft.
嗯，你知道吗，珍娜，那段采访，整段罗德尼·丹格菲尔德的喜剧即兴表演并不在拍摄剧本里。

928
00:47:02.200 --> 00:47:03.320
It's a whole other talking head.
原本是另一段采访。

929
00:47:03.520 --> 00:47:03.800
Huh.
哈。

930
00:47:04.060 --> 00:47:06.940
So I have to imagine they handed Steve a whole bunch of alts.
所以我猜他们给了史蒂夫很多备选方案。

931
00:47:07.060 --> 00:47:08.180
They would do that to us, right?
他们以前也会那样对我们，对吧？

932
00:47:08.620 --> 00:47:12.200
And this is the one that they picked because that is not the one in the script.
而这是他们最终选用的版本，因为它不在剧本里。

933
00:47:13.200 --> 00:47:13.600
Interesting.
有意思。

934
00:47:13.980 --> 00:47:15.180
Well, I liked this one.
嗯，我喜欢这一版。

935
00:47:15.360 --> 00:47:15.960
I did too.
我也喜欢。

936
00:47:16.140 --> 00:47:18.640
And I have to think Steve improvised a little.
我觉得史蒂夫肯定即兴发挥了一些。

937
00:47:18.800 --> 00:47:19.720
I think it was on the page.
我觉得那是剧本里写好的。

938
00:47:19.720 --> 00:47:21.980
But I can sort of see Steve doing his thing.
但我能想象出史蒂夫发挥他个人风格的样子。

939
00:47:22.320 --> 00:47:23.080
I'm sure.
我肯定。

940
00:47:23.560 --> 00:47:28.040
While that talking head was happening, everyone else is in the parking lot, you know?
在那段采访进行的同时，其他人都在停车场，你知道吗？

941
00:47:28.280 --> 00:47:29.380
They're heading home.
他们正准备回家。

942
00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:35.040
There is a wrap-up scene of the Dwight, Andy, Angela love triangle.
有一个关于德怀特、安迪和安吉拉三角恋的收尾场景。

943
00:47:35.560 --> 00:47:39.700
It's in the shooting draft, and it didn't make it to the deleted scenes.
它在拍摄剧本里，但没能进入删减片段。

944
00:47:39.920 --> 00:47:41.740
But Andy and Angela walk to the car.
安迪和安吉拉走向车子。

945
00:47:41.740 --> 00:47:48.200
They pass by Dwight, who is scraping off a Cornell sticker from the back window of the Xterra.
他们经过德怀特身边，他正在把一张康奈尔大学的贴纸从Xterra的后窗上刮下来。

946
00:47:48.580 --> 00:47:50.640
And Andy says, goodbye, old friend.
安迪说，再见了，老朋友。

947
00:47:50.880 --> 00:47:54.640
May all your roads be downhill and the wind be on your back windshield.
愿你前路皆是下坡，风儿常伴你的后挡风玻璃。

948
00:47:54.920 --> 00:47:56.680
And Angela's like, Andy.
安吉拉说，安迪。

949
00:47:57.220 --> 00:48:00.040
And Andy says, I can't believe Dwight would do me like that.
安迪说，我真不敢相信德怀特会那样对我。

950
00:48:00.180 --> 00:48:01.820
He took advantage of my kindness.
他利用了我的善良。

951
00:48:02.140 --> 00:48:05.060
And Angela says, he didn't take advantage of you.
安吉拉说，他并没有占你便宜。

952
00:48:05.220 --> 00:48:06.200
He bested you.
他是胜过了你。

953
00:48:11.980 --> 00:48:15.580
And she looks at Dwight like he's super hot.
而且她看德怀特的眼神，就像觉得他帅呆了一样。

954
00:48:16.900 --> 00:48:17.540
Yeah.
没错。

955
00:48:17.920 --> 00:48:22.940
Well, Angela, we should just call these deleted scenes feisty in the parking lot.
好吧，安吉拉，我们应该把这些删减片段统称为“停车场里的火药味”。

956
00:48:22.940 --> 00:48:29.580
Because I know that over by Pam and Jim's car, there is a scene that we shot that I believe
因为我知道在帕姆和吉姆的车那边，我们拍过一个场景，我相信

957
00:48:29.580 --> 00:48:36.880
is in the deleted scenes where Jim tells Pam the truth about Ryan and what Ryan said to him
它就在删减片段里，吉姆告诉了帕姆关于瑞安的真相，以及瑞安对他说了什么，

958
00:48:36.880 --> 00:48:40.460
and that he's gunning for him to maybe get fired or put him on notice.
还有瑞安正盯着他，想让他被解雇或者给他下最后通牒。

959
00:48:40.680 --> 00:48:42.860
And Pam is not having it.
而帕姆根本不吃这一套。

960
00:48:43.020 --> 00:48:45.260
Oh, I titled it Pam's Pissed.
哦，我把它命名为“帕姆发火了”。

961
00:48:45.420 --> 00:48:45.900
Yeah.
没错。

962
00:48:46.180 --> 00:48:48.060
And Sam, you got to play that clip.
萨姆，你得播放那个片段。

963
00:48:49.780 --> 00:48:51.260
Hey, what really happened today?
嘿，今天到底发生了什么？

964
00:48:51.540 --> 00:48:51.920
What do you mean?
什么意思？

965
00:48:52.160 --> 00:48:55.060
I mean, I don't need my glasses to know when something's stressing you out.
我是说，我不需要戴眼镜也能看出你什么时候压力很大。

966
00:48:55.220 --> 00:48:55.760
What happened today?
今天发生了什么？

967
00:48:58.460 --> 00:48:59.920
Ryan is trying to get rid of me.
瑞安想除掉我。

968
00:49:01.160 --> 00:49:04.640
He came in today to give me an official warning about my job performance.
他今天来给我发了一份关于我工作表现的正式警告。

969
00:49:05.080 --> 00:49:05.400
What?
什么？

970
00:49:06.720 --> 00:49:08.260
God, he's such a creep.
天哪，他真是个混蛋。

971
00:49:09.240 --> 00:49:10.800
That really pisses me off.
这真的让我火冒三丈。

972
00:49:11.420 --> 00:49:12.740
I'm going to bash his face in.
我要把他的脸砸烂。

973
00:49:12.880 --> 00:49:14.740
I'm going to bash his face in with a stale bagel.
我要用一块硬得像石头的百吉饼把他的脸砸烂。

974
00:49:14.940 --> 00:49:16.220
Then I'm going to throw a rock at his car.
然后我要往他的车上扔石头。

975
00:49:17.220 --> 00:49:18.780
Come on, we're going to New York right now.
来吧，我们现在就去纽约。

976
00:49:18.840 --> 00:49:19.240
I'm driving.
我来开车。

977
00:49:19.360 --> 00:49:21.180
If I hit him without my glasses, I don't think it's a crime.
如果我不戴眼镜撞了他，我觉得这不算犯罪。

978
00:49:21.740 --> 00:49:22.060
Great.
太棒了。

979
00:49:23.180 --> 00:49:25.200
God, I should have told you all about this sooner.
天哪，我早该把这一切都告诉你的。

980
00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:26.520
What a jerk.
真是个混蛋。

981
00:49:26.760 --> 00:49:27.720
What a jerk.
真是个混蛋。

982
00:49:29.200 --> 00:49:36.740
Can you imagine if they had left in the sex talk between Jim and Pam up at the top and
你能想象如果他们保留了开头吉姆和帕姆之间的性爱谈话，

983
00:49:36.740 --> 00:49:41.760
then this scene of Pam saying she's going to throw a rock at Ryan or maybe hit him with
然后接着是这个帕姆说要往瑞安身上扔石头，或者可能要用

984
00:49:41.760 --> 00:49:42.380
her car?
车撞他的场景，会是什么样吗？

985
00:49:42.840 --> 00:49:44.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

986
00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:46.720
And in the shooting draft, it was much shorter.
在拍摄剧本里，这段要短得多。

987
00:49:46.720 --> 00:49:48.760
You just said, I'm going to smash his face.
你当时只说了，“我要把他的脸砸烂”。

988
00:49:48.760 --> 00:49:50.600
And that was it, you know.
就这些，你知道的。

989
00:49:50.740 --> 00:49:54.000
But in this deleted scene, Pam is going off.
但在删减片段里，帕姆彻底爆发了。

990
00:49:54.260 --> 00:49:55.680
You do not mess with her, man.
伙计，你可别惹她。

991
00:49:56.000 --> 00:49:56.980
I guess not.
我想也是。

992
00:49:57.340 --> 00:49:59.420
Not after the night they had last night.
尤其是在他们昨晚共度良宵之后。

993
00:50:00.220 --> 00:50:01.660
The one night in heaven?
那“天堂一夜”？

994
00:50:02.080 --> 00:50:02.580
Yeah.
没错。

995
00:50:04.740 --> 00:50:05.260
Wowzers.
哇哦。

996
00:50:05.740 --> 00:50:10.300
Well, the tag for this episode brings us all the resolution we need.
好吧，这一集的结尾片段为我们带来了所需的一切结局。

997
00:50:10.300 --> 00:50:12.000
We're back in the conference room.
我们回到了会议室。

998
00:50:12.360 --> 00:50:19.640
Michael is proposing some more great ideas like a summer Christmas caroling sales event.
迈克尔正在提出一些更棒的点子，比如夏季圣诞颂歌销售活动。

999
00:50:19.920 --> 00:50:21.500
He throws to Stanley.
他转向斯坦利。

1000
00:50:21.840 --> 00:50:23.360
Stanley, what do you think?
斯坦利，你觉得怎么样？

1001
00:50:23.660 --> 00:50:28.080
Stanley says, I think it might be your best idea yet.
斯坦利说，我觉得这可能是你目前为止最好的主意了。

1002
00:50:28.620 --> 00:50:28.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1003
00:50:28.980 --> 00:50:33.360
And then Phyllis kind of laughs and says, that's the dumbest thing I've ever heard.
然后菲利斯笑了笑说，那是我听过最蠢的主意。

1004
00:50:33.360 --> 00:50:36.800
Michael says, everybody out except Phyllis.
迈克尔说，除了菲利斯，所有人都出去。

1005
00:50:41.280 --> 00:50:42.760
It's such a great tag.
这真是个很棒的标签。

1006
00:50:43.540 --> 00:50:45.280
Guys, that was Did I Stutter?
伙计们，刚才那是《我结巴了吗？》那一集。

1007
00:50:45.520 --> 00:50:47.780
I can't believe I'm about to say this, Angela.
安吉拉，我真不敢相信我竟然要说出这句话。

1008
00:50:47.960 --> 00:50:50.380
We are coming up on the end of season four.
我们快要看完第四季了。

1009
00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:52.220
We've just got a few more episodes.
只剩下最后几集了。

1010
00:50:52.580 --> 00:50:53.060
I know.
我知道。

1011
00:50:53.260 --> 00:50:56.440
Last night, I had to put a whole new disc in my DVD player.
昨晚，我不得不往DVD播放机里换了一张新光盘。

1012
00:50:56.980 --> 00:50:57.480
Wow.
哇。

1013
00:50:57.820 --> 00:51:01.520
You know it's serious when she's got to put a new disc in, guys.
伙计们，当她不得不换新光盘时，你就知道事情不简单了。

1014
00:51:01.680 --> 00:51:02.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1015
00:51:02.100 --> 00:51:04.960
I'm on my last disc for season four.
我正在看第四季的最后一张光盘。

1016
00:51:05.280 --> 00:51:07.060
It's going by so faSt.
时间过得太快了。

1017
00:51:07.200 --> 00:51:08.340
It's flying by.
简直是飞逝。

1018
00:51:08.660 --> 00:51:10.720
We'll be back next week with Job Fair.
下周我们将回来讨论《招聘会》那一集。

1019
00:51:10.940 --> 00:51:13.460
Thank you to Brent Forrester and to Leslie David Baker.
感谢布伦特·福雷斯特和莱斯利·大卫·贝克。

1020
00:51:13.780 --> 00:51:16.520
Thanks for texting us back about this episode.
谢谢你们回复短信讨论这一集。

1021
00:51:16.780 --> 00:51:21.180
And thanks to me for being a digital hoarder and having my shooting draft.
也谢谢我自己，作为一个数字囤积狂，还保留着拍摄剧本。

1022
00:51:21.740 --> 00:51:22.280
Yes.
没错。

1023
00:51:22.620 --> 00:51:23.560
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

1024
00:51:24.240 --> 00:51:25.320
All right, you guys.
好了，伙计们。

1025
00:51:25.460 --> 00:51:26.200
Have a great week.
祝你们度过愉快的一周。

1026
00:51:26.320 --> 00:51:27.200
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1027
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:31.920
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

